# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
*.egg

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Jupyter ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/**/*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Dataset (raw data not committed — see data/README.md for download instructions) ---
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md

# --- MLflow ---
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
mlflow.db

# --- Model artifacts (large binaries — don't commit trained models directly) ---
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.h5
*.pt
*.onnx
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
# Deliberate exception (Issue #80): the pooled M4 serving model. The rule above exists to
# keep *large* binaries out; this artifact is ~1.7 KB, is byte-for-byte reproducible from
# a fixed seed (so it is auditable, not opaque — its SHA-256 is in the manifest beside it),
# and is the one artifact the serving container needs at startup that cannot be
# regenerated without the 6.2 GB raw dataset. Reasoning: docs/serving_model_artifact.md.
!models/serving_model.joblib
!models/serving_model_manifest.json
# Deliberate exception (Issue #90): the M5 drift-detection baseline -- eight floats (four
# monitored features' pooled mean/std), directly human-diffable text, not an opaque
# binary. Same "large binaries only" reasoning as the model artifact above; this file is
# ~700 bytes. Reasoning: docs/monitoring_design.md Section 3.
!models/drift_baseline.json
# Deliberate exception (Issue #140): the trajectory archive Section 12 of
# docs/agent_design.md compares live bearings against -- 9,464 rows x 8 columns, 443 KB,
# measured rather than estimated. Same "large binaries only" reasoning as the two above.
# Unlike them this one is not human-diffable, and that was weighed rather than waved past:
# the same rows as CSV are over a megabyte and no more reviewable in a diff, since nobody
# reads a 9,464-line numeric diff either way (Section 12's own argument). What makes it
# auditable is the manifest beside it, which carries a hash of the *data* as well as of the
# file -- so a re-encode on a different pyarrow build is distinguishable from a changed
# number. It is committed for the reason #86 committed real signal: regenerating it needs
# the 6.2 GB raw dataset, so without it a fresh clone has no reference data at all.
!models/trajectory_archive.parquet
!models/trajectory_archive_manifest.json

# --- Docker ---
*.log

# --- Monitoring (local Prometheus/Grafana state, if run locally) ---
prometheus_data/
grafana_data/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Test / coverage ---
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Claude Code conversation exports (/export writes YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS-<slug>.txt to cwd) ---
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
# --- Claude Code local settings (not shared, machine-specific) ---
.claude/settings.local.json
